  "answer": "The authors propose H‑Net, a U‑Net‑inspired hierarchical sequence model that compresses input sequences with a chunking layer, processes them in a main network, and restores the original resolution with a dechunking layer [Dynamic Chunking for End-to-End Hierarchical Sequence Modeling, arXiv:2507.07955v2, PDF p. 5]. Unlike traditional U‑Net designs, H‑Net dispenses with fixed‑size pooling operations, determining chunk boundaries dynamically instead [Dynamic Chunking for End-to-End Hierarchical Sequence Modeling, arXiv:2507.07955v2, PDF p. 5].",
